Nature of the derivative work and changes
-----------------------------------------

go-plocate was produced by an LLM agent (Anthropic's Claude) as a partial
reimplementation of plocate in the Go programming language. It is NOT a verbatim
copy; it is a translation and reduction. Specifically:

  * Only the database READ/QUERY path was ported. The database-building tools
    (updatedb, plocate-build) and all of their supporting code (filesystem
    scanning, bind-mount handling, configuration parsing, the TurboPFor encoder)
    were NOT ported.

  * The TurboPFor posting-list decoder is a port of the scalar (non-SIMD) code
    path of plocate's turbopfor.cpp, limited to the single codec plocate emits
    (delta-plus-1, interleaved, 128-value blocks, 32-bit document IDs).

  * Regular-expression matching (-r/--regexp, --regex) was deliberately omitted.

  * I/O uses memory mapping and synchronous reads rather than io_uring; output
    serialization, the trigram parser, the glob matcher (fnmatch), and the
    directory-visibility check were reimplemented in Go to match the observable
    behavior of upstream plocate.

The file COPYING (the GNU General Public License, version 2) is reproduced from
the upstream plocate distribution.

Third-party references
----------------------

  * Michael Stapelberg's TurboPFor analysis was used as documentation of the
    on-disk posting-list format:
    https://michael.stapelberg.ch/posts/2019-02-05-turbopfor-analysis/

  * Stapelberg's goturbopfor (https://github.com/stapelberg/goturbopfor,
    Apache-2.0) targets a different TurboPFor variant and was NOT copied into
    this work; it was consulted only as a cross-reference for the byte layout.
    No Apache-2.0 code is included here.
